test.yaml:11:17: the cache saves "~/.npmrc", which can hold credentials (the token of an npm registry). a cache can be restored by other workflows of the repository, so what is in it is not secret. remove the path from the cache, or cache what the step downloads and not the configuration with the token [cache-poisoning]
test.yaml:18:17: the cache saves ".git", which can hold credentials (the git config of the checkout keeps the token of actions/checkout unless persist-credentials is false). a cache can be restored by other workflows of the repository, so what is in it is not secret. remove the path from the cache, or cache what the step downloads and not the configuration with the token [cache-poisoning]
